# UI interaction

Follow `UI_INTERACTION_PRINCIPLES.md`.

- Do not leave the current reading/library context for a local action.
- Local actions (memo, citation, term, workspace picker) use a Popover.
- Larger temporary work (export, figure zoom) uses a Sheet / Overlay.
- Paper-wide lists use the Inspector. Body actions must not auto-open it.
- Modals are only for irreversible decisions.
- New routes are only for real place changes (Library / Reader / Workspace / Settings).
- Closing a temporary surface must restore scroll, outline, inspector, search, and the open paper.
- Shared Element Transitions: when the same object changes place or size (e.g. figure zoom), morph continuously from the inline frame — do not cut to a new overlay.
- Reuse existing components. Do not rebuild UI that already follows these rules.
